          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These triangles are seen to have the same shape, but not the same size. Hence, two triangles that have the same set of angles need not be congruent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.283,
            0.703,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measuring Two Sides and the Included Angle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.311,
            0.574,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ΔABC and ΔXYZ are two triangles such that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.348,
            0.743,
            0.367
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "AB = XY = 6\\  cm , AC = XY = 5\\  cm , and \\angle A = \\angle X = 30^{\\circ}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.376,
            0.357,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are they congruent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.396,
            0.846,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To check this, we need to see if there can exist non-congruent triangles with the given measurements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.434,
            0.847,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These measurements correspond to the case of two sides and the included angle. We have seen how to construct a triangle given these measurements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.501,
            0.673,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Construct a triangle having the above measurements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.533,
            0.847,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Compare it with the triangles constructed by your classmates. Are the triangles all congruent? Explain why all such triangles with these measurements are congruent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.591,
            0.846,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, when two sides and the included angle of two triangles are equal, the two triangles are congruent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.629,
            0.846,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is referred to as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SAS (Side Angle Side)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition for congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.686,
            0.734,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measuring Two Sides and a Non-included Angle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.712,
            0.683,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What if two sides and a non-included angle are equal?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.74,
            0.573,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ΔABC and ΔXYZ are two triangles such that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.778,
            0.742,
            0.797
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "AB = XY = 6\\  cm , AC = XY = 4\\  cm , and \\angle B = \\angle Y = 30^{\\circ}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.807,
            0.356,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are they congruent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.835,
            0.846,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can there exist non-congruent triangles having these measurements? Construct and find out."
            }
          ]
